# C1. Full Database Schema DDL — All Phase 1 Schemas

**Status:** Blocking — foundation for all subsequent implementation work
**Platform:** Batac City LGU Platform
**Scope:** Complete PostgreSQL DDL for all tables in schemas `iam`, `organization`, `documents`, `workflow`, `tracking`, `records`, `notifications`, `audit` (Phase 1). `search_meta`, `portal`, `reporting` are reserved as empty namespaces only (Phase 2/3 — no tables per source instruction).
**Engine target:** PostgreSQL 16. Every statement in this document has been executed against a live PostgreSQL 16 instance from a clean database with `ON_ERROR_STOP=1`, including trigger and constraint behavior tests — see [Validation Notes](#validation-notes).
**Sources:** `main--schema-ddl-source-reference.md`, `h3-numbering-series-configuration-specification.md`, `d4-domain-class-diagram.md`, `h2-document-type-catalog-with-jsonb-metadata-schema.md`, `b2-module-boundary-and-internal-api-contracts.md`, `b4-workflow-engine-specification.md`.


## Table of Contents

- [L34–L82] Conventions and Design Decisions — Global database design resolutions for primary keys, tenant column, soft-delete columns, cross-schema logical keys, and PostgreSQL enum handling.
- [L83–L110] Preamble — Schema creation statements for all Phase 1 schemas and reserved namespaces, plus pgcrypto extension setup.
- [L111–L138] Shared Infrastructure — DDL and indexing for the shared public.event_bus_dead_letters table to track failed event handling.
- [L139–L322] Schema: iam — DDL for authentication, users, credentials, session constraints, refresh tokens, role/permission assignments, and MFA/TOTP storage.
- [L323–L487] Schema: organization — DDL for hierarchical offices, positions, employee records, assignment mappings, delegation grants, and legislative committee memberships.
- [L488–L884] Schema: documents — DDL for document metadata, series numbering, versions, attachments, signatures, sponsorships, Panlalawigan reviews, publications, and sequence functions.
- [L885–L1210] Schema: workflow — DDL for workflow definitions, steps, transitions, instances, step execution history, urgent bypasses, committee reports, SP sessions, and agendas.
- [L1211–L1277] Schema: tracking — DDL for physical document tracking, including QR code associations, current custody locations, and append-only routing history logs.
- [L1278–L1374] Schema: records — DDL for document retention schedules, classification rules, post-workflow record catalogs, archive entry logs, and legal disposition controls.
- [L1375–L1435] Schema: notifications — DDL for dispatching notifications, containing channel-specific message templates, recipient details, status events, and delivery attempts logs.
- [L1436–L1474] Schema: audit — DDL for the system audit trail, specifying an append-only table for event logs with SHA-256 chain hashes and HMACs.
- [L1475–L1571] Roles, Grants, and Row-Level Security — PostgreSQL role declarations, database privilege grants, and Row-Level Security (RLS) policies enforcing office-level isolation and IT admin content exclusion.
- [L1572–L1593] 2026 Numbering Sequences — Initialization of the eleven gapless document numbering sequences required specifically for the 2026 calendar year.
- [L1594–L1599] Reserved Phase 2/3 Schemas — Documentation outlining planned tables for search metadata, public portal request forms, and reporting schemas reserved for future phases.
- [L1600–L1627] Invariant and Non-Negotiable Compliance Checklist — A traceability checklist mapping the sixteen compliance invariants and non-negotiables to their specific database design implementations.
- [L1628–L1648] Open Items Requiring Confirmation — A registry of twelve design gaps, enum inferences, or conflicting source specifications requiring stakeholder sign-off.
- [L1649–L1661] Validation Notes — Validation reports confirming clean execution of DDL on PostgreSQL 16 and testing results for triggers and helper functions.

