## Schema: iam

Authentication, session control, JWT-adjacent token storage, role/permission resolution. ABAC office-scoping and Tier 1/2/3 authorization are application-layer concerns (Authorization Tiers, B2); no dedicated ABAC policy table exists in any source document, so none is invented here — `iam.role_assignments.office_scope_id` is the one piece of schema support the source material grounds for office-scoped rules.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: iam
-- ============================================================================

-- Login-capable identities only. Personal/employment data (name, office,
-- position) lives in organization.employees; see Employee.hasAccount (D4),
-- which is a 0..1 relationship from Employee to User.
CREATE TABLE iam.users (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    username            TEXT NOT NULL,
    email               TEXT NOT NULL,
    status              TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE'
                            CHECK (status IN ('ACTIVE','INACTIVE','SUSPENDED','DEACTIVATED')),
    mfa_enabled         BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_users_city_username UNIQUE (city_id, username),
    CONSTRAINT uq_users_city_email UNIQUE (city_id, email)
);

-- 1:1 with users (D4: User "1" *-- "1" Credential).
CREATE TABLE iam.credentials (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    password_hash       TEXT NOT NULL,
    last_changed_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_credentials_user UNIQUE (user_id)
);

-- One active session per user (Session Management: "Concurrent sessions:
-- One active session per user"; "New login from different device: Logs
-- out previous session"). Enforced via the partial unique index below as
-- the DB-level second line of defense; the application is responsible for
-- terminating the prior session in the same transaction as creating a new
-- one.
CREATE TABLE iam.sessions (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    session_token_hash  TEXT NOT NULL,
    ip_address          INET NULL,
    user_agent          TEXT NULL,
    issued_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    expires_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    last_active_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    terminated_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    terminated_by       UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    termination_reason  TEXT NULL
                            CHECK (termination_reason IN ('user_action','forced','timeout')),
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_sessions_token_hash UNIQUE (session_token_hash)
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_sessions_one_active_per_user
    ON iam.sessions (user_id)
    WHERE is_active = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE INDEX idx_sessions_user ON iam.sessions (user_id);

-- Refresh token storage: server-side DB, hashed value (Auth Architecture
-- Requirements). Never the raw token.
CREATE TABLE iam.refresh_tokens (
    id              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    session_id      UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.sessions (id),
    token_hash      TEXT NOT NULL,
    issued_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    expires_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    is_revoked      BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    revoked_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by      UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_refresh_tokens_hash UNIQUE (token_hash)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_refresh_tokens_user ON iam.refresh_tokens (user_id);

CREATE TABLE iam.roles (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                TEXT NOT NULL,
    code                TEXT NOT NULL,
    description         TEXT NULL,
    -- [Inference] Design aid for Invariant #12 (Platform Administrator role
    -- cannot be combined with an operational/document-processing role).
    -- Full enforcement is application-layer role-assignment validation per
    -- source; this flag supports that check.
    is_platform_admin   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_roles_city_code UNIQUE (city_id, code)
);

CREATE TABLE iam.permissions (
    id              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    resource        TEXT NOT NULL,
    action          TEXT NOT NULL,
    description     TEXT NULL,
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by      UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_permissions_city_resource_action UNIQUE (city_id, resource, action)
);

-- Junction: Role *--* Permission : grants (D4).
CREATE TABLE iam.role_permissions (
    id              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    role_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.roles (id),
    permission_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.permissions (id),
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by      UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_role_permissions UNIQUE (role_id, permission_id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_role_permissions_role ON iam.role_permissions (role_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_role_permissions_permission ON iam.role_permissions (permission_id);

-- Junction: User *--* Role : assigned (D4). office_scope_id supports ABAC
-- office-scoped rules ("Pure RBAC cannot express office-scoped rules");
-- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema; no constraint).
CREATE TABLE iam.role_assignments (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    role_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.roles (id),
    office_scope_id     UUID NULL,
    assigned_by         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    assigned_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    revoked_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    revoked_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_role_assignments_user ON iam.role_assignments (user_id) WHERE is_active = true;
CREATE INDEX idx_role_assignments_role ON iam.role_assignments (role_id);

-- TOTP designed from day one; not enabled in Phase 1; required in Phase 2
-- for Mayor, SP Secretary, Department Heads, Platform Administrator, IT
-- Admin (Auth Architecture Requirements). See Conventions section above
-- for the source conflict this table resolves.
CREATE TABLE iam.mfa_records (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    method              TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'TOTP' CHECK (method IN ('TOTP')),
    secret_encrypted    TEXT NOT NULL,
    is_enabled          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    enabled_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    last_verified_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL REFERENCES iam.users (id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_mfa_records_user_method UNIQUE (user_id, method)
);
```

## Schema: organization

Office hierarchy, positions, employees, assignments, delegation grants, and committees. `Committee`/`CommitteeMembership` are placed here per D4's explicit note ("they are not generic Office entities... they have term-bound membership and produce CommitteeReport entities that interact with the Workflow module"), but are not `organization.offices` rows.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: organization
-- ============================================================================

-- office_type values are [Inference] -- no enumerated list is given in any
-- source document for D4's OfficeType attribute. EXTERNAL is structurally
-- required because incoming-letter (SPR) documents record the external
-- sender as originating_office_id, which is a row in this table.
CREATE TABLE organization.offices (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                TEXT NOT NULL,
    code                TEXT NOT NULL,
    office_type         TEXT NOT NULL
                            CHECK (office_type IN ('EXECUTIVE','LEGISLATIVE','DEPARTMENT','EXTERNAL')),
    parent_office_id    UUID NULL REFERENCES organization.offices (id),
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema; no constraint)
    CONSTRAINT uq_offices_city_code UNIQUE (city_id, code)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_offices_parent ON organization.offices (parent_office_id);

-- authority_level is left as unconstrained TEXT: D4 declares Position.level
-- as an AuthorityLevel enum but no value list is given anywhere in source,
-- and (unlike OfficeType) there is no structural requirement strong enough
-- to justify inventing specific values. Confirm with stakeholders before
-- adding a CHECK constraint. See Open Items.
CREATE TABLE organization.positions (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    office_id           UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.offices (id),
    title               TEXT NOT NULL,
    code                TEXT NOT NULL,
    authority_level     TEXT NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_positions_city_code UNIQUE (city_id, code)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_positions_office ON organization.positions (office_id);

-- user_id is logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema; no constraint).
-- Employee "1" --> "0..1" User : hasAccount (D4) -- not every employee logs
-- in. UNIQUE partial index enforces the implied inverse: a User account
-- belongs to exactly one Employee.
CREATE TABLE organization.employees (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    user_id             UUID NULL,
    employee_number     TEXT NOT NULL,
    first_name          TEXT NOT NULL,
    last_name           TEXT NOT NULL,
    email               TEXT NOT NULL,
    phone_number        TEXT NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_employees_city_number UNIQUE (city_id, employee_number)
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_employees_user_id ON organization.employees (user_id) WHERE user_id IS NOT NULL;

CREATE TABLE organization.assignments (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    employee_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    position_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.positions (id),
    office_id           UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.offices (id),
    start_date          DATE NOT NULL,
    end_date            DATE NULL,
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT chk_assignments_dates CHECK (end_date IS NULL OR end_date >= start_date)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_assignments_employee ON organization.assignments (employee_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_assignments_position ON organization.assignments (position_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_assignments_office ON organization.assignments (office_id);

-- Invariant #16: one active designation per person at any time. References
-- Employee, not User, matching D4's DelegationGrant relationships (B2's
-- DelegationSummary TypeScript type names the same fields delegatingUserId/
-- delegatedToUserId, but that is read as informal API naming, not a
-- directive to FK against iam.users from this schema). Open-ended
-- delegations are prohibited, so end_date is NOT NULL.
CREATE TABLE organization.delegation_grants (
    id                          UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                     UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    delegated_by_employee_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    delegated_to_employee_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    office_id                   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.offices (id),
    position_id                 UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.positions (id),
    scope_description           TEXT NOT NULL,
    legal_basis                 TEXT NULL,
    start_date                  DATE NOT NULL,
    end_date                    DATE NOT NULL,
    is_active                   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    designation_document_id     UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    revoked_by_employee_id      UUID NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    revoked_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                  UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT chk_delegation_dates CHECK (end_date > start_date),
    CONSTRAINT chk_delegation_not_self CHECK (delegated_by_employee_id <> delegated_to_employee_id)
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_delegation_one_active_per_delegatee
    ON organization.delegation_grants (delegated_to_employee_id)
    WHERE is_active = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE INDEX idx_delegation_delegator ON organization.delegation_grants (delegated_by_employee_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_delegation_delegatee ON organization.delegation_grants (delegated_to_employee_id);

-- D4 multiplicity is "1" (mandatory) on Committee --> Employee : chairedBy,
-- taken literally rather than relaxed to 0..1.
CREATE TABLE organization.committees (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                    TEXT NOT NULL,
    code                    TEXT NOT NULL,
    chaired_by_employee_id  UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_committees_city_code UNIQUE (city_id, code)
);

CREATE TABLE organization.committee_memberships (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    committee_id        UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.committees (id),
    employee_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES organization.employees (id),
    committee_role      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (committee_role IN ('CHAIRMAN','VICE_CHAIRMAN','MEMBER')),
    start_date          DATE NOT NULL,
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_committee_membership_active
    ON organization.committee_memberships (committee_id, employee_id)
    WHERE is_active = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE INDEX idx_committee_memberships_employee ON organization.committee_memberships (employee_id);
```

## Schema: documents

Document lifecycle, immutable versioning, two-stage series numbering, attachments, signatures, sponsorships, and the Panlalawigan review / publication satellite tables. This is the largest and most heavily cross-referenced schema; see the Conventions section above for the reasoning behind several structural decisions made here (numbers-vs-control-numbers, the denormalized-plus-historical numbering design, and the two tables added beyond B2's canonical seven).

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: documents
-- ============================================================================

-- owning_module is a routing/ownership label, not a literal schema
-- reference -- 'portal' is valid even though no portal.* tables exist in
-- Phase 1 (see Conventions: "Citizen Complaint and Document Request Form
-- live in documents, not portal").
CREATE TABLE documents.document_types (
    id                          UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                     UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                        TEXT NOT NULL,
    code                        TEXT NOT NULL,
    owning_module               TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (owning_module IN ('workflow','organization','portal')),
    number_series_id            UUID NULL, -- FK added below, after documents.number_series exists
    has_preliminary_numbering   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    control_number_deferred     BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    requires_publication        BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    retention_schedule_id       UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> records.retention_schedules.id (cross-schema)
    classification_default      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (classification_default IN ('PUBLIC','INTERNAL','CONFIDENTIAL','RESTRICTED')),
    public_visibility_rule      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (public_visibility_rule IN
                                    ('TITLE_AND_FIRST_PAGE_PUBLIC','NOT_PUBLIC','COMPLAINANT_RESTRICTED','REQUESTER_RESTRICTED')),
    required_step_types         TEXT[] NULL,
    metadata_schema             JSONB NULL,
    is_active                   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                  UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_document_types_city_code UNIQUE (city_id, code),
    -- Invariant #11 as a DB-level second line of defense, alongside the
    -- application validation constraint the source also calls for.
    CONSTRAINT chk_document_types_retention_before_activation
        CHECK (is_active = false OR retention_schedule_id IS NOT NULL)
);

-- document_type_id is nullable specifically to accommodate
-- panlalawigan_review_log, which this DDL does not model as a document
-- type (see Conventions). series_type, sp_ordinal, and
-- sequence_name_prefix are [Inference] additions per H3 Implementation
-- Notes 1 and the sequence-naming table (Table 2).
CREATE TABLE documents.number_series (
    id                              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    series_key                      TEXT NOT NULL,
    document_type_id                UUID NULL REFERENCES documents.document_types (id),
    series_type                     TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (series_type IN ('LEGISLATIVE','ADMINISTRATIVE')),
    prefix                          TEXT NULL,
    sp_ordinal                      TEXT NULL, -- [Inference -- H3 Note 1] separates the "7" in 7SP from the
                                                -- rendered prefix string, so an administration change is a
                                                -- single field update rather than three data edits.
    sequence_padding                SMALLINT NOT NULL,
    sequence_name_prefix            TEXT NOT NULL, -- e.g. 'ns_nch' (H3 Table 2); used by next_sequence_value()
    preliminary_format              TEXT NULL,
    final_format                    TEXT NOT NULL,
    delimiter                       TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ' ',
    resets_annually                 BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    year_format                     TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'YYYY',
    authority_office_id             UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema)
    preliminary_assignment_event    TEXT NULL,
    final_assignment_event          TEXT NOT NULL,
    deferred_final_assignment       BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    phase                           TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '1' CHECK (phase IN ('1','1B')),
    created_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                      UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_number_series_city_key UNIQUE (city_id, series_key)
);

ALTER TABLE documents.document_types
    ADD CONSTRAINT fk_document_types_number_series
    FOREIGN KEY (number_series_id) REFERENCES documents.number_series (id);

-- Required columns per H2 ("the required columns for the documents.documents
-- DDL"). preliminary_number / final_number / control_number /
-- number_series_id are the DENORMALIZED current values for fast reads; the
-- full assignment history lives in documents.numbers below.
CREATE TABLE documents.documents (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_type_id        UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.document_types (id),
    title                   TEXT NOT NULL,
    lifecycle_state         TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Draft' CHECK (lifecycle_state IN
                                ('Draft','Submitted','In-Workflow','Pending Approval','Completed','Released','Archived','Disposed','Cancelled')),
    classification_level    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (classification_level IN ('PUBLIC','INTERNAL','CONFIDENTIAL','RESTRICTED')),
    qr_tracking_number      UUID NOT NULL,
    preliminary_number      TEXT NULL,
    final_number            TEXT NULL,
    control_number          TEXT NULL,
    number_series_id        UUID NULL REFERENCES documents.number_series (id),
    originating_office_id   UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema)
    owned_by_office_id      UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema)
    drafted_by_employee_id  UUID NULL,     -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    created_by              UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    workflow_instance_id    UUID NULL,     -- logical FK -> workflow.instances.id (cross-schema)
    retention_schedule_id   UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> records.retention_schedules.id (cross-schema)
    version_number          INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    metadata                JSONB NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,
    tsv                     tsvector NULL, -- [Phase 1] FTS vector for title (ADR-B2-5)
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_documents_qr_tracking_number UNIQUE (qr_tracking_number)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_documents_type ON documents.documents (document_type_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_lifecycle_state ON documents.documents (lifecycle_state);
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_originating_office ON documents.documents (originating_office_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_owned_by_office ON documents.documents (owned_by_office_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_workflow_instance ON documents.documents (workflow_instance_id);

-- "JSONB -- Admin-configurable document metadata... Use GIN indexes. Query
-- with @> operator and ->> accessors" (PostgreSQL Non-Negotiables), plus
-- the three specific expression indexes H2 calls out as minimum targets.
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_metadata_gin ON documents.documents USING GIN (metadata);
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_metadata_certified_urgent ON documents.documents ((metadata ->> 'certified_urgent'));
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_metadata_has_penalty ON documents.documents ((metadata ->> 'has_penalty_provision'));
CREATE INDEX idx_documents_metadata_outcome_state ON documents.documents ((metadata ->> 'outcome_state'));

-- "Check constraints for state transitions -- Enforce valid workflow state
-- transitions at the DB level as a second line of defense" (PostgreSQL
-- Non-Negotiables). The transition graph below is [Inference], derived
-- from the stated lifecycle order plus the explicitly described
-- "approval" step behavior (approve / reject / return for revision) and
-- the terminal-state framing of Cancelled/Archived/Disposed. "Cancelled...
-- reachable from any active state" is read as the states before Released
-- (Draft through Completed); confirm the exact allowed transitions with
-- the workflow engine team before relying on this as a hard gate.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION documents.check_lifecycle_transition()
RETURNS TRIGGER
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $fn$
DECLARE
    v_allowed BOOLEAN := false;
BEGIN
    IF NEW.lifecycle_state IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.lifecycle_state THEN
        v_allowed := CASE OLD.lifecycle_state
            WHEN 'Draft'             THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Submitted','Cancelled')
            WHEN 'Submitted'         THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('In-Workflow','Cancelled')
            WHEN 'In-Workflow'       THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Pending Approval','Cancelled')
            WHEN 'Pending Approval'  THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Completed','In-Workflow','Cancelled')
            WHEN 'Completed'         THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Released','Cancelled')
            WHEN 'Released'          THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Archived')
            WHEN 'Archived'          THEN NEW.lifecycle_state IN ('Disposed')
            WHEN 'Disposed'          THEN false
            WHEN 'Cancelled'         THEN false
            ELSE false
        END;

        IF NOT v_allowed THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION 'invalid document lifecycle transition: % to %', OLD.lifecycle_state, NEW.lifecycle_state;
        END IF;
    END IF;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$fn$;

CREATE TRIGGER trg_documents_lifecycle_transition
    BEFORE UPDATE ON documents.documents
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION documents.check_lifecycle_transition();

-- FTS trigger to maintain the tsv column (ADR-B2-5)
CREATE TRIGGER trg_documents_tsv_update
    BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE OF title ON documents.documents
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION tsvector_update_trigger(tsv, 'pg_catalog.english', title);

-- Historical/event-sourced ledger of every number assignment (D4's
-- DocumentNumber, with NumberType extended to add CONTROL -- see
-- Conventions). Each reassignment is a new row; PRELIMINARY rows flip
-- is_current = false when superseded, never edited in place.
CREATE TABLE documents.numbers (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    number_series_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.number_series (id),
    number_type         TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (number_type IN ('PRELIMINARY','FINAL','CONTROL')),
    number_value        TEXT NOT NULL,
    year                INTEGER NOT NULL,
    sequence_number     INTEGER NOT NULL,
    is_current          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    assigned_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    assigned_by         UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    superseded_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    -- H3 Implementation Note 2: unique constraint scoped to
    -- (series, year, sequence) -- not the rendered format string, because
    -- a resolution and an ordinance can legitimately share a rendered
    -- number like "7SP 2026-05" under different series.
    CONSTRAINT uq_numbers_series_year_seq UNIQUE (number_series_id, year, sequence_number)
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_numbers_one_current_per_type
    ON documents.numbers (document_id, number_type)
    WHERE is_current = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE INDEX idx_numbers_document ON documents.numbers (document_id);

-- "Final numbers (after the Draft prefix removed) are immutable -- no
-- override path exists for any role" (main reference document, Numbering
-- Architecture Decisions). Extended here to CONTROL numbers for the same
-- reason.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION documents.check_number_immutability()
RETURNS TRIGGER
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $fn$
BEGIN
    IF OLD.number_type IN ('FINAL','CONTROL') AND OLD.number_value IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.number_value THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'final and control numbers are immutable once assigned: % %', OLD.number_type, OLD.number_value;
    END IF;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$fn$;

CREATE TRIGGER trg_numbers_immutability
    BEFORE UPDATE ON documents.numbers
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION documents.check_number_immutability();

-- file_key is UUID, never the original filename, per Invariant #5
-- ("S3-compatible API only; UUID file keys").
CREATE TABLE documents.versions (
    id                              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id                     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    version_number                  INTEGER NOT NULL,
    file_key                        UUID NOT NULL,
    mime_type                       TEXT NOT NULL,
    page_count                      INTEGER NULL,
    scan_quality                    TEXT NULL CHECK (scan_quality IN ('GOOD','FAIR','POOR')),
    ocr_processed                   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    ocr_text                        TEXT NULL,
    tsv                             tsvector NULL, -- [Phase 1] FTS vector for OCR text (ADR-B2-5)
    -- "the system flags the scanned image for manual verification by a
    -- Records Officer before acceptance as the official copy" (Versioning).
    requires_manual_verification    BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    verified_by                     UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    verified_at                     TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_by                      UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    created_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                      UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_versions_document_number UNIQUE (document_id, version_number)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_versions_document ON documents.versions (document_id);

-- FTS trigger to maintain the tsv column (ADR-B2-5)
CREATE TRIGGER trg_versions_tsv_update
    BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE OF ocr_text ON documents.versions
    FOR EACH ROW
    EXECUTE FUNCTION tsvector_update_trigger(tsv, 'pg_catalog.english', ocr_text);

-- CertificationOfUrgency is realized as a row here, not as its own table
-- (D4 Relationship Note 6). source_document_id lets one Certification of
-- Urgency Document (its own documents.documents row, type
-- CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY) be attached to several measures without
-- re-uploading the file, since "a single Certification of Urgency can
-- cover multiple measures in the same session."
CREATE TABLE documents.attachments (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    attachment_type     TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (attachment_type IN ('CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY','COMMITTEE_REPORT','TRANSMITTAL_LETTER','SCAN','OTHER')),
    file_key             UUID NULL,
    source_document_id  UUID NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    mime_type            TEXT NULL,
    description          TEXT NULL,
    uploaded_by          UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    created_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by            UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT chk_attachments_file_or_source CHECK (file_key IS NOT NULL OR source_document_id IS NOT NULL)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_attachments_document ON documents.attachments (document_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_attachments_source_document ON documents.attachments (source_document_id);

CREATE TABLE documents.signatures (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    signature_type          TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (signature_type IN ('PRESIDING_OFFICER','MAYOR','SP_SECRETARY','VICE_MAYOR','COMMITTEE_CHAIR')),
    signed_by_employee_id   UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    signed_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    is_wet_ink              BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_signatures_document ON documents.signatures (document_id);

-- Distinct from Document.draftedBy (one drafter); a measure may have
-- several councilor sponsors. Required for the Index of Ordinances
-- tracked fields (H2, footnote on Transmittal Letter section).
CREATE TABLE documents.document_sponsorships (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    sponsor_employee_id UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    sponsorship_type    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (sponsorship_type IN ('PRINCIPAL_AUTHOR','CO_AUTHOR','INTRODUCER','CO_INTRODUCER')),
    order_of_priority   INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    created_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by            UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_sponsorships UNIQUE (document_id, sponsor_employee_id, sponsorship_type)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_sponsorships_document ON documents.document_sponsorships (document_id);

-- Added beyond B2's seven-table canonical list -- see Conventions
-- ("Entities given a table beyond B2's canonical short list"). control_no
-- is populated from the panlalawigan_review_log series via
-- number_series_id, not from a documents.documents row.
CREATE TABLE documents.panlalawigan_reviews (
    id                          UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                     UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id                 UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    number_series_id            UUID NULL REFERENCES documents.number_series (id),
    control_no                  TEXT NULL,
    subject                     TEXT NULL,
    transmitted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    received_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    date_referred                DATE NULL,
    date_approved_disapproved   DATE NULL,
    outcome                     TEXT NULL CHECK (outcome IN ('VALID','VALID_IN_PART','RETURNED','OPERATIVE_IN_ITS_ENTIRETY','DEEMED_APPROVED')),
    panlalawigan_resolution_no  TEXT NULL,
    remarks                      TEXT NULL,
    days_elapsed                 INTEGER NULL,
    created_at                    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at                     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                      TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                       UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_panlalawigan_reviews_document ON documents.panlalawigan_reviews (document_id);

-- Added beyond B2's seven-table canonical list -- see Conventions. 0..1
-- from Document per D4, hence the unique constraint on document_id.
CREATE TABLE documents.publication_records (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES documents.documents (id),
    newspaper           TEXT NOT NULL,
    publication_date    DATE NOT NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_publication_records_document UNIQUE (document_id)
);

-- Operationalizes "Sequences for gapless document numbering -- Use
-- PostgreSQL sequences with appropriate configuration per series per
-- year" ergonomically. Assumes the target year's sequence already exists
-- (created via the annual numbering-sequence migration -- an ops concern
-- H3 explicitly excludes from DDL scope, not handled by this function).
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION documents.next_sequence_value(p_series_key TEXT, p_year INTEGER)
RETURNS INTEGER
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $fn$
DECLARE
    v_prefix    TEXT;
    v_seq_name  TEXT;
    v_next      BIGINT;
BEGIN
    SELECT sequence_name_prefix INTO v_prefix
    FROM documents.number_series
    WHERE series_key = p_series_key AND deleted_at IS NULL;

    IF v_prefix IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'unknown or deleted number series: %', p_series_key;
    END IF;

    v_seq_name := 'documents.' || v_prefix || '_' || p_year::text || '_seq';

    BEGIN
        EXECUTE format('SELECT nextval(%L)', v_seq_name) INTO v_next;
    EXCEPTION WHEN undefined_table THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'sequence % does not exist yet; run the annual numbering-sequence migration for year % before assigning numbers', v_seq_name, p_year;
    END;

    RETURN v_next::INTEGER;
END;
$fn$;
```

## Schema: workflow

The generic workflow engine (definitions, versions, steps, transitions, running instances and step instances, the append-only event log, and the Certified-Urgent bypass queue) exactly as specified in B4, plus the SP-Session/Committee-Report tables D4 places in this schema as "workflow-adjacent" but which B4 does not cover.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: workflow
-- ============================================================================

-- Native enums: B4 explicitly names these three types with an "_enum"
-- suffix and gives complete, authoritative value lists, unlike every other
-- domain-value column in this document (see Conventions: Enum strategy).
CREATE TYPE workflow.workflow_step_type_enum AS ENUM
    ('action','approval','multi_referral','decision','notification','termination','parallel_split','parallel_join');

CREATE TYPE workflow.workflow_instance_status_enum AS ENUM
    ('active','suspended','stuck','completed','cancelled');

CREATE TYPE workflow.workflow_step_status_enum AS ENUM
    ('pending','active','completed','bypassed','cancelled','failed');

-- At most one active definition per document type (B4 DB-Level Constraint
-- #1, partial unique index given verbatim in source).
CREATE TABLE workflow.definitions (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_type_id    UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.document_types.id (cross-schema)
    name                TEXT NOT NULL,
    description         TEXT NULL,
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_by          UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_definitions_one_active_per_doctype
    ON workflow.definitions (document_type_id)
    WHERE is_active = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

-- Immutable published snapshot. status is a GENERATED column reconciling
-- D4's DefinitionStatus enum (Draft/Published/Deprecated) with B4's actual
-- schema, which tracks the same information via two nullable timestamps
-- rather than a stored status -- see Conventions.
CREATE TABLE workflow.definition_versions (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    definition_id       UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.definitions (id),
    version_number      INTEGER NOT NULL,
    snapshot            JSONB NOT NULL,
    published_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    published_by        UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    deprecated_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    is_current          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    status               TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (
                            CASE
                                WHEN deprecated_at IS NOT NULL THEN 'Deprecated'
                                WHEN published_at IS NOT NULL THEN 'Published'
                                ELSE 'Draft'
                            END
                          ) STORED,
    created_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by           UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_definition_versions_def_number UNIQUE (definition_id, version_number)
);

-- At most one current version per definition (B4 DB-Level Constraint #2,
-- partial unique index given verbatim in source).
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_definition_versions_one_current
    ON workflow.definition_versions (definition_id)
    WHERE is_current = true;

CREATE INDEX idx_definition_versions_definition ON workflow.definition_versions (definition_id);

-- Denormalized from definition_versions.snapshot for query efficiency; the
-- snapshot JSONB remains authoritative on conflict (B4).
CREATE TABLE workflow.steps (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    definition_version_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.definition_versions (id),
    step_key                TEXT NOT NULL,
    step_type               workflow.workflow_step_type_enum NOT NULL,
    label                   TEXT NOT NULL,
    config                  JSONB NULL,
    position                INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    is_start                BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_steps_version_key UNIQUE (definition_version_id, step_key)
);

-- "Exactly one step per definition version must have is_start = true.
-- Validated at publish time" (B4) -- enforced here as a DB-level second
-- line of defense via partial unique index.
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_steps_one_start_per_version
    ON workflow.steps (definition_version_id)
    WHERE is_start = true AND deleted_at IS NULL;

CREATE INDEX idx_steps_definition_version ON workflow.steps (definition_version_id);

CREATE TABLE workflow.transition_rules (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    definition_version_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.definition_versions (id),
    from_step_id            UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.steps (id),
    to_step_id              UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.steps (id),
    condition_expression    TEXT NULL,
    outcome_filter          TEXT NULL,
    priority                INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    label                   TEXT NULL,
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_transition_rules_from_step ON workflow.transition_rules (from_step_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_transition_rules_definition_version ON workflow.transition_rules (definition_version_id);

-- definition_version_id is pinned at creation (Invariant #4) and has "no
-- application-layer update path... except via engine.migrateInstance" per
-- B4's own DB-Level Constraints table (#5), which explicitly calls for a
-- migration comment rather than a DB trigger -- so none is added here.
-- lapse_status (named in B2's WorkflowInstanceSummary type) is
-- intentionally NOT a stored column: B4's authoritative instances column
-- table omits it, and it is derivable from the terminal step_instance's
-- outcome code (LAPSED_INTO_LAW / DEEMED_APPROVED_PANLALAWIGAN).
CREATE TABLE workflow.instances (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    definition_version_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.definition_versions (id),
    document_id             UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    status                  workflow.workflow_instance_status_enum NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',
    -- Mutable state store; schema enforced by the application (Zod, per
    -- B4), not by a PostgreSQL CHECK constraint. See B4's "Context Schema"
    -- reference for the full key set (mayor_action, panlalawigan_outcome,
    -- certified_urgent, publication fields, etc).
    context                 JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,
    sla_deadline            TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    sla_breached_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    started_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    completed_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_by              UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_instances_document ON workflow.instances (document_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_instances_definition_version ON workflow.instances (definition_version_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_instances_sla_active ON workflow.instances (sla_deadline) WHERE status = 'active';

-- Encoder/final-approver distinct-user invariant (#13) is explicitly
-- application-layer only per B4 ("not a DB constraint") -- no trigger
-- added here, by design.
CREATE TABLE workflow.step_instances (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    instance_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.instances (id),
    step_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.steps (id),
    status              workflow.workflow_step_status_enum NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    assigned_to         JSONB NULL,
    started_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    completed_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    outcome             TEXT NULL,
    outcome_comment     TEXT NULL,
    -- Heavily used by multi_referral steps; null for action steps. See
    -- B4's "step_instances.metadata Shape" reference for the structure.
    metadata            JSONB NULL,
    sla_deadline        TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    sla_breached_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    bypassed_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    bypassed_by         UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); null = system-triggered
    bypass_reason       TEXT NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_step_instances_instance ON workflow.step_instances (instance_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_step_instances_step ON workflow.step_instances (step_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_step_instances_metadata_gin ON workflow.step_instances USING GIN (metadata);

-- Append-only event log. No deleted_at/deleted_by -- see Conventions
-- ("Soft delete") -- and UPDATE/DELETE are revoked from
-- workflow_app_user at the PostgreSQL grant level in the Roles section
-- below, per B4's explicit instruction.
CREATE TABLE workflow.workflow_events (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    instance_id         UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.instances (id),
    step_instance_id    UUID NULL REFERENCES workflow.step_instances (id),
    event_type          TEXT NOT NULL,
    actor_id            UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); null for system events
    actor_type          TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (actor_type IN ('user','system','scheduler')),
    payload             JSONB NOT NULL,
    occurred_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_workflow_events_instance ON workflow.workflow_events (instance_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_workflow_events_step_instance ON workflow.workflow_events (step_instance_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_workflow_events_occurred_at ON workflow.workflow_events (occurred_at);

-- Tracks deferred Certified Urgent bypasses for instances whose
-- multi_referral step has not yet activated when the Certification is
-- logged (B4).
CREATE TABLE workflow.pending_certified_urgent_bypasses (
    id                          UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                     UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    instance_id                 UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.instances (id),
    step_key                    TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'committee_referral',
    certification_document_id   UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    created_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    applied_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    applied_to_step_instance_id UUID NULL REFERENCES workflow.step_instances (id),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                  UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_pending_bypasses_instance ON workflow.pending_certified_urgent_bypasses (instance_id);

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Workflow-adjacent: SP Session and Committee Report. D4 places these in
-- the workflow schema explicitly ("Includes: SP Session and Committee
-- Report -- workflow-adjacent"); B4 does not cover them since it scopes
-- only the generic, reusable engine mechanics.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- 1:1 with a multi_referral step instance -- represents the eventual
-- unified report for that step, not each individual committee submission
-- (those live in step_instances.metadata.submissions per B4).
CREATE TABLE workflow.committee_reports (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    step_instance_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.step_instances (id),
    submitted_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    is_unified          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    is_accepted         BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    accepted_by         UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    accepted_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    content             TEXT NULL,
    document_id         UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_committee_reports_step_instance UNIQUE (step_instance_id)
);

-- Junction for CommitteeReport *--* Committee : signedBy (D4) -- a unified
-- report from a multi_referral step is signed by every assigned committee.
CREATE TABLE workflow.committee_report_signatures (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    committee_report_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.committee_reports (id),
    committee_id            UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.committees.id (cross-schema)
    signed_by_employee_id   UUID NULL,     -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    signed_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_committee_report_signatures UNIQUE (committee_report_id, committee_id)
);

CREATE TABLE workflow.sp_sessions (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    session_number          INTEGER NOT NULL,
    session_date            DATE NOT NULL,
    session_type            TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (session_type IN ('REGULAR','SPECIAL')),
    presided_by_employee_id UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    present_count           INTEGER NULL,
    quorum_achieved         BOOLEAN NULL,
    created_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_sp_sessions_city_number UNIQUE (city_id, session_number)
);

CREATE TABLE workflow.session_attendances (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    sp_session_id       UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.sp_sessions (id),
    employee_id         UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    is_present          BOOLEAN NOT NULL,
    absence_reason      TEXT NULL CHECK (absence_reason IN ('OB','SICK_LEAVE','VACATION_LEAVE','ABSENT')),
    recorded_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by             UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_session_attendance UNIQUE (sp_session_id, employee_id),
    CONSTRAINT chk_attendance_reason CHECK (is_present = true OR absence_reason IS NOT NULL)
);

CREATE TABLE workflow.order_of_business (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    sp_session_id       UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.sp_sessions (id),
    generated_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    cutoff_date         DATE NOT NULL,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by            UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_order_of_business_session UNIQUE (sp_session_id)
);

-- item_type values are [Inference], grounded in the explicit First/Second/
-- Third Reading + Committee Report vocabulary used throughout the source
-- (Order of Business content is described as "all documents scheduled for
-- the upcoming session's First Reading").
CREATE TABLE workflow.order_of_business_items (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    order_of_business_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow.order_of_business (id),
    document_id             UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    item_order              INTEGER NOT NULL,
    item_type                TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (item_type IN ('FIRST_READING','SECOND_READING','THIRD_READING','COMMITTEE_REPORT','OTHER')),
    is_red_flagged            BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    created_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                   UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_oob_items_order UNIQUE (order_of_business_id, item_order)
);
```

## Schema: tracking

QR code identity, the physical/custody tracking record per document, and the append-style routing history. Deliberately kept separate from `documents.documents.lifecycle_state`: "Physical custody | Tracked separately from digital workflow status" (main reference document, DTS).

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: tracking
-- ============================================================================

-- tracking_id holds the same UUID value as documents.documents.
-- qr_tracking_number (D4 Relationship Note 9: "Both hold the same UUID
-- value"). Assigned at secretariat logging, before the preliminary number.
CREATE TABLE tracking.qr_codes (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    tracking_id         UUID NOT NULL,
    qr_image_file_key   UUID NULL,
    assigned_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by          UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_qr_codes_tracking_id UNIQUE (tracking_id),
    CONSTRAINT uq_qr_codes_document UNIQUE (document_id)
);

-- current_status is intentionally free TEXT, not CHECK-constrained against
-- documents.documents.lifecycle_state -- the two are explicitly separate
-- state machines (physical custody vs. digital workflow status).
CREATE TABLE tracking.tracking_records (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    qr_code_id          UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES tracking.qr_codes (id),
    current_status      TEXT NULL,
    current_location    TEXT NULL,
    last_moved_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    created_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_tracking_records_document UNIQUE (document_id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_tracking_records_qr_code ON tracking.tracking_records (qr_code_id);

-- Field shape follows B2's RoutingEntry TypeScript interface
-- (fromOfficeId/toOfficeId/actorId/actionDescription/timestamp) rather
-- than D4's looser fromLocation/toLocation strings, since B2 is explicitly
-- the "Shared Types -- Inform Column Definitions" source.
CREATE TABLE tracking.routing_entries (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    tracking_record_id  UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES tracking.tracking_records (id),
    from_office_id      UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema)
    to_office_id        UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.offices.id (cross-schema)
    actor_id            UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); null = system action
    action_description  TEXT NOT NULL,
    occurred_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_at            TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by              UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_routing_entries_tracking_record ON tracking.routing_entries (tracking_record_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_routing_entries_occurred_at ON tracking.routing_entries (occurred_at);
```

## Schema: records

Retention schedules, classification rules, the post-workflow record catalog, archive entries, and dispositions. Implemented in full per the Conventions note above (this schema is not reserved-only, despite B2's module-phase label).

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: records
-- ============================================================================

-- document_type_id is intentionally NOT a column here: the governing
-- direction is documents.document_types.retention_schedule_id ->
-- records.retention_schedules.id, so this table stays a standalone
-- catalog rather than holding a redundant inverse reference.
CREATE TABLE records.retention_schedules (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                    TEXT NOT NULL,
    retention_period_years  INTEGER NULL,
    is_permanent            BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    disposition_rule        TEXT NULL,
    legal_basis              TEXT NULL,
    configured_by            UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); Platform Admin, Tier 2
    created_at                TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                   UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT chk_retention_period CHECK (is_permanent = true OR retention_period_years IS NOT NULL)
);

CREATE TABLE records.classification_rules (
    id                              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    retention_schedule_id           UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES records.retention_schedules (id),
    condition_expression            TEXT NOT NULL,
    target_classification_level     TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (target_classification_level IN ('PUBLIC','INTERNAL','CONFIDENTIAL','RESTRICTED')),
    priority                         INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    created_at                        TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                         TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                          UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_classification_rules_schedule ON records.classification_rules (retention_schedule_id);

-- record_type is left as unconstrained TEXT -- D4 declares RecordType as
-- an enum but gives no value list anywhere in source. See Open Items.
CREATE TABLE records.records (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id         UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    record_number       TEXT NOT NULL,
    record_type         TEXT NOT NULL,
    physical_location    TEXT NULL,
    formalized_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    created_by             UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    created_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                  UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_records_city_number UNIQUE (city_id, record_number),
    CONSTRAINT uq_records_document UNIQUE (document_id)
);

CREATE TABLE records.archive_entries (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id             UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    archived_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    archive_location        TEXT NULL,
    archived_by_employee_id UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    created_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                   UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_archive_entries_document UNIQUE (document_id)
);

-- disposition_type distinguishes standard disposition from RA 10173 PII
-- erasure, which requires formal legal review (City Legal / DPO) before
-- erasure -- enforced here via CHECK as a second line of defense alongside
-- the application-layer process.
CREATE TABLE records.dispositions (
    id                          UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                     UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    document_id                 UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> documents.documents.id (cross-schema)
    disposed_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    reason                      TEXT NOT NULL,
    legal_basis                 TEXT NULL,
    disposition_type            TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'STANDARD' CHECK (disposition_type IN ('STANDARD','RA10173_ERASURE')),
    legal_review_by             UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema)
    legal_review_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    authorized_by_employee_id   UUID NOT NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema); Records Officer
    created_at                   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                    TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                     UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_dispositions_document UNIQUE (document_id),
    CONSTRAINT chk_disposition_erasure_review CHECK (disposition_type <> 'RA10173_ERASURE' OR legal_review_by IS NOT NULL)
);
```

## Schema: notifications

Templates, dispatched notification events, and per-attempt delivery logs. Phase 1 recipients are internal employees only (D4 Relationship Note 14); `recipient_email`/`recipient_phone` exist to support external recipients such as complaint respondents. Per ADR-B2-4, all respondent notices route through this module to log delivery attempts in `delivery_log`.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: notifications
-- ============================================================================

CREATE TABLE notifications.templates (
    id                  UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id             UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    name                TEXT NOT NULL,
    channel             TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (channel IN ('IN_APP','EMAIL','SMS')),
    subject_template    TEXT NULL,
    body_template       TEXT NOT NULL,
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    created_by           UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); Platform Admin, Tier 2
    created_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                 UUID NULL,
    CONSTRAINT uq_templates_city_name_channel UNIQUE (city_id, name, channel)
);

CREATE TABLE notifications.notification_events (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    template_id             UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES notifications.templates (id),
    channel                 TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (channel IN ('IN_APP','EMAIL','SMS')),
    recipient_employee_id   UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> organization.employees.id (cross-schema)
    recipient_email         TEXT NULL,
    recipient_phone         TEXT NULL,
    template_data           JSONB NULL,
    status                  TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Pending' CHECK (status IN ('Pending','Sent','Failed','Cancelled')),
    triggered_at             TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    source_event_type        TEXT NULL,
    created_at                 TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                   UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_notification_events_template ON notifications.notification_events (template_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_notification_events_recipient ON notifications.notification_events (recipient_employee_id);

CREATE TABLE notifications.delivery_log (
    id                      UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id                 UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    notification_event_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES notifications.notification_events (id),
    attempt_count            INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    status                   TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('Delivered','Bounced','Failed')),
    delivered_at              TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    error_message             TEXT NULL,
    created_at                  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    deleted_at                   TIMESTAMPTZ NULL,
    deleted_by                    UUID NULL
);

CREATE INDEX idx_delivery_log_event ON notifications.delivery_log (notification_event_id);
```

## Schema: audit

Append-only, hash-chained, HMAC-signed activity log. The application — never the database — computes `chain_hash` and `hmac` using Node's built-in `crypto` module; this schema only stores the result.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA: audit
-- ============================================================================

-- Gives the hash chain an unambiguous, monotonic "previous record" pointer
-- independent of wall-clock timestamp ordering ([Inference] addition; the
-- source describes the chain mechanism but not how "previous" is resolved
-- at the storage layer).
CREATE SEQUENCE audit.events_sequence_seq AS BIGINT INCREMENT 1 START 1;

-- No deleted_at/deleted_by, no updated_at -- see Conventions ("Soft
-- delete"). UPDATE and DELETE are revoked from audit_app_user at the
-- PostgreSQL grant level below (Invariant #3).
CREATE TABLE audit.events (
    id              UUID NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    city_id         UUID NOT NULL DEFAULT '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid,
    sequence_number BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT nextval('audit.events_sequence_seq'),
    event_type      TEXT NOT NULL,
    actor_id        UUID NULL, -- logical FK -> iam.users.id (cross-schema); null for system events
    target_id       UUID NULL,
    target_type     TEXT NULL,
    payload         JSONB NOT NULL,
    chain_hash      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (chain_hash ~ '^[a-f0-9]{64}$'),
    hmac            TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (hmac ~ '^[a-f0-9]{64}$'),
    hmac_key_version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    occurred_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_audit_events_sequence ON audit.events (sequence_number);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_events_city_occurred ON audit.events (city_id, occurred_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_events_actor ON audit.events (actor_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_events_target ON audit.events (target_id);
```

## Roles, Grants, and Row-Level Security

Implements the two explicit PostgreSQL non-negotiables that cut across schemas: office-level data isolation via RLS, and IT admin having no access to document content. Actual login credentials/passwords are provisioned via the secrets manager / Terraform per Invariant #15 ("Backup credentials separate from production credentials") and are out of scope for DDL; only the roles and their grants are defined here.

"IT admin has no document content access" (Invariant #10) and "IT admin must NOT have read access to confidential or restricted document content" (Authorization Model) are reconciled as two distinct rules: IT admin is blocked entirely from the file-content tables (`documents.versions`, `documents.attachments`), and is additionally blocked by RLS from even the metadata row on `documents.documents` when its classification is `CONFIDENTIAL` or `RESTRICTED`.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- ROLES, GRANTS, AND ROW-LEVEL SECURITY
-- ============================================================================

CREATE ROLE app_runtime_user NOLOGIN;
CREATE ROLE it_admin_user NOLOGIN;
CREATE ROLE audit_app_user NOLOGIN;
-- workflow_app_user is named explicitly in B4's REVOKE instruction for
-- workflow.workflow_events; granted to app_runtime_user rather than kept
-- fully separate, since the application runtime is the actor that writes
-- workflow events day to day.
CREATE ROLE workflow_app_user NOLOGIN;

GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA iam, organization, documents, workflow, tracking, records, notifications
    TO app_runtime_user;

GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA iam TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA organization TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA documents TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA workflow TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA tracking TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA records TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA notifications TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON public.event_bus_dead_letters TO app_runtime_user;
-- No DELETE grant anywhere above: Invariant #2 ("no hard deletes") is
-- reinforced at the grant level, not only by application code discipline.

GRANT workflow_app_user TO app_runtime_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON workflow.workflow_events TO workflow_app_user;
REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON workflow.workflow_events FROM workflow_app_user;

-- Invariant #3: audit log INSERT-only at the DB role level.
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit TO audit_app_user;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit.events TO audit_app_user;
REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON audit.events FROM audit_app_user;
GRANT USAGE ON SEQUENCE audit.events_sequence_seq TO audit_app_user;

-- Invariant #10 / Authorization Model: IT admin has no document CONTENT
-- access, full stop -- not even for public documents.
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA documents TO it_admin_user;
GRANT SELECT, UPDATE ON documents.documents TO it_admin_user;
REVOKE ALL ON documents.versions, documents.attachments FROM it_admin_user;

ALTER TABLE documents.documents ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Office-level data isolation enforced at the DB engine ("PostgreSQL
-- Non-Negotiables"). The application sets app.current_office_id (and,
-- for elevated roles that legitimately need cross-office visibility,
-- app.bypass_office_isolation) via SET at the start of each request/
-- transaction.
CREATE POLICY documents_office_isolation ON documents.documents
    FOR SELECT
    TO app_runtime_user
    USING (
        owned_by_office_id = current_setting('app.current_office_id', true)::uuid
        OR current_setting('app.bypass_office_isolation', true) = 'true'
    );

-- IT admin may see metadata rows for non-confidential/restricted
-- documents (e.g. to diagnose a stuck workflow) but never confidential or
-- restricted ones, and can never see file content at all (revoked above).
CREATE POLICY documents_it_admin_no_confidential ON documents.documents
    FOR SELECT
    TO it_admin_user
    USING (classification_level NOT IN ('CONFIDENTIAL','RESTRICTED'));

-- UPDATE is granted to it_admin_user above for operational fixes (e.g.
-- correcting a stuck workflow_instance_id), but WITH CHECK (false) means
-- no UPDATE can actually commit until a specific, narrower policy is
-- added for the exact operational fields IT admin is allowed to touch --
-- a deliberately closed default rather than an open one.
CREATE POLICY documents_it_admin_metadata_only_update ON documents.documents
    FOR UPDATE
    TO it_admin_user
    USING (true)
    WITH CHECK (false);

-- Supports "IT/security admin can force-terminate any session" while
-- keeping ordinary session visibility scoped to the owning user.
ALTER TABLE iam.sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY sessions_own_or_admin ON iam.sessions
    FOR SELECT
    TO app_runtime_user
    USING (
        user_id = current_setting('app.current_user_id', true)::uuid
        OR current_setting('app.current_role_tier', true) IN ('IT_ADMIN','SECURITY_ADMIN')
    );
```

## 2026 Numbering Sequences

One PostgreSQL sequence per series per year ("Sequences for gapless document numbering," PostgreSQL Non-Negotiables; H3 Table 2). Only the current year's eleven sequences are created here; subsequent years are created by an annual migration following the same `ns_{prefix}_{YEAR}_seq` naming pattern — explicitly an operations/migration-scheduling concern that H3 excludes from DDL scope, not handled automatically by `documents.next_sequence_value()`.

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- 2026 NUMBERING SEQUENCES
-- ============================================================================

CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_sp_resolution_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_sp_ordinance_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_sp_appropriation_ordinance_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_nch_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_nosp_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_designation_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_letters_received_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_letters_sent_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_memo_outgoing_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_memo_incoming_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
CREATE SEQUENCE documents.ns_panlalawigan_review_log_2026_seq AS INTEGER INCREMENT 1 START 1;
```

## Reserved Phase 2/3 Schemas

Per the main reference document's explicit instruction: "`search_meta`, `portal`, and `reporting` are Phase 2/3. Reserve in the schema map but do not implement tables in Phase 1 DDL." The namespaces are created in the [Preamble](#preamble) above; no tables are created in any of the three. `search_meta` will hold `index_metadata`/`index_jobs`; `portal` will hold `public_documents`/`citizen_requests`/`complaints`/`announcements`; `reporting` will hold `report_definitions`/`schedules`/`outputs` — all deferred to their respective phases.

---

## Invariant and Non-Negotiable Compliance Checklist

| # | Invariant / Non-Negotiable | DDL Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Schema-per-module; no cross-schema FKs | Every cross-schema reference is a plain `UUID` column with an inline logical-FK comment; zero `REFERENCES` clauses cross a schema boundary anywhere in this document |
| 2 | Soft-delete everywhere; no hard deletes | `deleted_at`/`deleted_by` on every table except `audit.events` and `workflow.workflow_events` (justified exception, see Conventions); no `DELETE` grant given to `app_runtime_user` |
| 3 | Audit log INSERT-only at DB role level | `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON audit.events FROM audit_app_user` |
| 4 | Workflow instance pins to definition version at creation | `workflow.instances.definition_version_id NOT NULL`, no DB-level update guard per B4's explicit instruction (application-layer only, via `engine.migrateInstance`) |
| 5 | S3-compatible API only; UUID file keys | `documents.versions.file_key` and `documents.attachments.file_key` are `UUID`, never filename `TEXT` |
| 6 | UUID v4 primary keys everywhere | `id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()` on every table |
| 7 | `TIMESTAMPTZ` for all timestamps | Applied to every timestamp column without exception |
| 8 | `city_id UUID NOT NULL` in all core entity tables | Applied to every table, defaulted to the Batac City placeholder constant |
| 9 | Numbering assigned at defined lifecycle event only | Application/workflow-engine constraint per source; `documents.numbers` and the triggers support but do not themselves enforce event timing |
| 10 | IT admin has no document content access | `REVOKE ALL ON documents.versions, documents.attachments FROM it_admin_user`; RLS additionally blocks confidential/restricted rows on `documents.documents` |
| 11 | Document type must have retention schedule before activation | `CHECK (is_active = false OR retention_schedule_id IS NOT NULL)` on `documents.document_types` |
| 12 | Platform Administrator role cannot be combined with operational roles | Application-layer role-assignment validation per source; `iam.roles.is_platform_admin` flag added as a design aid |
| 13 | Encoder and final approver of same document cannot be the same user | Explicitly application-layer only per B4; no DB constraint added, by design |
| 14 | Workflow constraints per document type (legally mandated minimum steps) | `documents.document_types.required_step_types`; enforced by the workflow editor at definition-authoring time, per source |
| 15 | Backup credentials separate from production credentials | Out of DDL scope — infrastructure/Terraform concern |
| 16 | One active designation per person at any time | `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON organization.delegation_grants (delegated_to_employee_id) WHERE is_active = true AND deleted_at IS NULL` |
| — | JSONB for admin-configurable metadata, GIN-indexed | `documents.documents.metadata JSONB` + general GIN index + 3 targeted expression indexes |
| — | Row-Level Security for office-level isolation | `documents_office_isolation` policy on `documents.documents`; `sessions_own_or_admin` policy on `iam.sessions` |
| — | Append-only audit log | Grant-level `REVOKE` on `audit.events`, no soft-delete columns |
| — | Check constraints for state transitions | `documents.check_lifecycle_transition()` trigger; `CHECK` constraints on every status/classification/type column |
| — | One PostgreSQL sequence per numbering series per year | Eleven `documents.ns_*_2026_seq` sequences + `documents.next_sequence_value()` helper |

---

## Open Items Requiring Confirmation

These are the points where source documents conflicted outright, or where an attribute was declared but no value list or table location was ever given. Each is resolved with a stated, defensible default above so the DDL is runnable now, but each should be confirmed with stakeholders before Production Rollout.

| Item | Conflict / Gap | Resolution Taken | Confirm With |
|---|---|---|---|
| `iam.mfa_records` | D4 excludes `MfaRecord` from its Phase 1 entity list ("(Phase 2)"); B2 and the main schema map both list it as a Phase 1 `iam` table | Table created now, rows not expected until Phase 2 | Whoever owns the Phase 1/Phase 2 cutover plan for MFA |
| `records` schema phase | B2 labels the Records module "Phase: 2... schema reserved in Phase 1 migration"; main doc and D4 both treat it as full Phase 1 | Full DDL implemented now; only bulk-op/disposition application logic assumed Phase 2 | Whoever owns the Phase 1 delivery scope for Records |
| Citizen Complaint / Document Request data location | Main doc says `portal` is Phase 3, reserved-only; H2 footnote says portal is "partially initialized" in Phase 1 | Both document types live in `documents.documents` with JSONB metadata; no `portal.*` tables created | H2's author, to confirm the footnote is stale |
| `documents.documents.control_number` vs. `final_number` | H2 lists both as separate columns; main doc's prose sometimes uses "control number" loosely for what H3 calls a series' final number | `control_number` reserved for Letters Received/Sent (SPR/SPS) only; everything else uses `final_number` | Whoever owns H2/H3 reconciliation |
| `panlalawigan_review_log` entity classification | H3 explicitly flags this as unresolved | Modeled as `documents.panlalawigan_reviews` + a `number_series` row with no associated `document_types` row | H3's author |
| `documents.panlalawigan_reviews`, `documents.publication_records` | Not in B2's seven-table canonical list for `documents`; present as D4 entities with independent fields | Added as two extra tables | Whoever owns B2's canonical table list, to confirm it was meant as a floor, not a ceiling |
| `OfficeType` values | D4 declares the enum; no value list given anywhere | `[Inference]` CHECK: `EXECUTIVE, LEGISLATIVE, DEPARTMENT, EXTERNAL` | Organization module owner |
| `AuthorityLevel` values | D4 declares the enum; no value list given anywhere | Left unconstrained `TEXT`, no CHECK added | Organization module owner |
| `RecordType` values | D4 declares the enum; no value list given anywhere | Left unconstrained `TEXT`, no CHECK added | Records module owner |
| `OrderOfBusinessItemType` values | D4 declares the enum; no value list given anywhere | `[Inference]` CHECK: `FIRST_READING, SECOND_READING, THIRD_READING, COMMITTEE_REPORT, OTHER` | Workflow module owner |
| `documents.documents.lifecycle_state` transition graph | No explicit transition matrix given anywhere; only the linear order plus terminal-state framing | Trigger-enforced graph derived by inference (see inline comment on the trigger) | Workflow engine owner, before treating this trigger as a hard gate in production |
| `sequence_padding` for `letters_sent` (SPS) | H3 itself flags this: "3-digit padding may be required... confirm with SP Secretariat before finalising" | Kept at 2 digits as H3's table specifies, padding is enforced at the application formatting layer, not by a DB constraint | SP Secretariat, per H3's own footnote |

---

## Validation Notes

Every statement in this document — all `CREATE SCHEMA`, `CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX`, `CREATE SEQUENCE`, `CREATE FUNCTION`, `CREATE TRIGGER`, `CREATE ROLE`, `GRANT`/`REVOKE`, `ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`, and `CREATE POLICY` — was executed against a clean PostgreSQL 16 database with `psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1`, in the order presented in this document, with zero errors on a full, repeated, clean run (52 tables created across the 8 Phase 1 schemas).

In addition to a clean execution pass, the following behaviors were specifically exercised with live `INSERT`/`UPDATE` statements and confirmed correct:

- `documents.check_lifecycle_transition()` accepts a valid transition (`Draft` → `Submitted`) and rejects an invalid one (`Submitted` → `Released`) with a clear error.
- `documents.check_number_immutability()` rejects an attempt to change a `FINAL` number's value after assignment.
- `uq_numbers_one_current_per_type` (the partial unique index enforcing one current number per type per document) correctly rejects a second concurrently-current `PRELIMINARY` row for the same document.
- `documents.next_sequence_value()` correctly resolves a series key to its backing per-year sequence and returns successive values.
- `workflow.definition_versions.status` (the generated column) correctly derives `Draft`, `Published`, and `Deprecated` from `published_at`/`deprecated_at` as those columns are set.

This does not substitute for review against the live application's actual query patterns, nor for a security review of the RLS policies and role grants, which are illustrative of the required mechanisms (office isolation, IT-admin content exclusion, audit/event append-only enforcement) rather than a complete authorization model.
